WEBVTT

NOTE understanding-vwc: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.496
Three different numbers
wear the label VWC.

V0-2
00:00:05.596 --> 00:00:09.300
Knowing which one you are
reading explains most surprises.

V1a-1
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.693
When the scan date is today, Avg.

V1a-2
00:00:15.793 --> 00:00:20.310
VWC is the mean moisture TurfRad
measured across that station.

V1b-1
00:00:20.873 --> 00:00:25.079
It is a measurement, and it is the
number the calculation prefers.

V1b-2
00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:27.793
A current scan: black text, today's date.

V2a-1
00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:38.094
When the scan is not current,
Spatial Adjust falls back to a modelled

V2a-2
00:00:38.194 --> 00:00:41.846
value carried forward from the
last scan and the weather since.

V2b-1
00:00:42.396 --> 00:00:47.120
It is shown in grey italics so
you can tell it apart at a glance.

V2b-2
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.726
Station 7AP1 has no current scan;
the value shown is modelled.

V3a-1
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:03.661
Target VWC is a whole number from
0 to 50 that you set per station.

V3a-2
00:01:03.761 --> 00:01:06.660
Higher targets ask for more water.

V3b-1
00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:10.966
It is the only VWC on the
row you can type into.

V4a-1
00:01:18.823 --> 00:01:21.616
Subtract the working
VWC from the target and

V4a-2
00:01:21.716 --> 00:01:24.763
you have the deficit the
calculation must close.

V4b-1
00:01:25.273 --> 00:01:30.320
Add today's ET, cap it at the daily
maximum, and express it against the Lynx

V4b-2
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.203
reference amount. Target minus measured,
per station, is the whole idea.

V5a-1
00:01:42.396 --> 00:01:46.302
At hole and area level the same two
columns show averages rather than

V5a-2
00:01:46.402 --> 00:01:50.876
readings, and the scan date column shows
the most recent scan beneath that row.

V5b-1
00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:54.360
A grey calculator icon
on a hole or area row

V5b-2
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.790
means at least one station
beneath it is modelled.
